From bb443aa678af4c7623544bbc524a8a3d284df488 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:04:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] asahi: lay out M5 uniform ranges in dwords, as the M5
 program loader needs

The M5 graphics program builder (agx_build_agx3_graphics_program) moves
uniform dwords and refuses a push range that starts at an odd half
("push range shape"), but agx_nir_layout_uniforms only aligned ranges
for G17P. A fragment shader that samples a texture (one 16-bit lod_bias
half) and also reads a 16-bit root sysval (no_epilog_discard and
provoking_vertex, for discard or flat inputs) got the second range at
an odd uniform, so its program was never built and every draw using it
was dropped. Alacritty's text shader is that shape: every frame was
discarded and its windows stayed black on the M5 Pro.

Request dword ranges on every M5 part too.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_state.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_state.c b/src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_state.c
index 2653aea86e2..339797c5c54 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_state.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_state.c
@@ -2016,11 +2016,13 @@ agx_compile_nir(struct agx_device *dev, nir_shader *nir,
          compiled->g17p_texture_resources
             ? AGX_ABI_G17P_TEXTURE_POINTER_HALFS
             : 0;
-      /* G17P's Ioto loader moves uniform dwords: lay the ranges out so
-       * that each starts at an even half and covers an even count. */
+      /* G17P's Ioto loader and the M5 program builder move uniform dwords
+       * (agx_build_agx3_graphics_program refuses an odd range): lay the
+       * ranges out so that each starts at an even half and covers an even
+       * count. */
       NIR_PASS(_, nir, agx_nir_layout_uniforms, compiled,
                &key.reserved_preamble, uniform_base,
-               agx_native_graphics(dev));
+               agx_native_graphics(dev) || agx_chip_g17_m5(dev->chip));
       if (agx_native_graphics(dev))
          NIR_PASS(_, nir, agx_nir_lower_g17p_storage_records,
                   texture_descriptor_size);
